            <ArticleTitle>[Boutonneuse fever in tourists as a model for clinical diagnosis of rickettsioses (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>209-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Case histories of boutonneuse fever are described in order to exemplify major characteristics of most rickettsioses: recent travel history, feverish illness with severe headache, skin eruptions and histological findings. Up-to-date informations concerning the epidemiologic situation of typhus, scrub typhus and Rocky Mountain spotted fever are given. The characteristics of Q fever and the possibility of rickettsial laboratory infections are pointed out.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
